      "text": "The water cycle describes how water moves continuously between the ocean, the atmosphere and the land. Heat from the sun evaporates water from the sea surface into vapor that rises high into the sky. As the vapor cools it condenses into tiny droplets that gather to form clouds. When the droplets grow heavy enough they fall back to the ground as rain or snow, and rivers eventually carry that water back to the ocean, closing the loop."
