      "text": "A volcano forms where molten rock called magma rises from deep inside the planet toward the surface. Magma collects in a chamber beneath the crust, and mounting pressure forces it upward through cracks. During an eruption the magma bursts out as lava, ash and gas, which pile up around the vent. Layer after layer of cooled lava slowly builds the cone-shaped mountain we recognize as a volcano."
